\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 , matching workers to companies and offering subsidies to participating businesses. UN experts warned in January that the programmes can amount to forced labour and are being used to "forcibly re-engineer" Uyghur identity. Many workers are monitored and Mandarin lessons and ideological training are standard parts of the programmes.}
